# Optional per-client settings.
#
# The client id used in hostname prefixes is the filename (without .env). It must
# be EGT's casino identifier, lowercased with the underscore removed:
#     DN_BAHISBEY -> dnbahisbey.env
# Derive it from the casinokey rather than the Casino column - they differ where a
# brand has been renamed (DN_ILKBAHIS carries casinokey 174_ORJINBET and routes as
# dnorjinbet).
#
# CASINO_ID is written into /api/game/url-extended/<client> as casinoId.
# Defaults to the client filename if unset, which is almost never right.
# CASINO_ID="174_BAHISBEY"
#
# HOST_SUFFIX selects which naming form is advertised for this brand. Unset means
# "-bgsp", which is correct for most brands. Set it to the empty string for a
# brand EGT have already migrated off the legacy convention:
#     HOST_SUFFIX=""
# Both hostname forms are served regardless; this only decides which one goes in
# the URL payload. Check which one a brand answers to with:
#     curl -sk --connect-to "<label>.probe.example:443:p4.fpp-ong.com:443" \
#          -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://<label>.probe.example/
# Any HTTP code means it routes; 000 means it does not.
